greetings brave adventurers seekers of  knowledge explorers of the great unknown  no doubt by now you've heard the stories  of the noble lord theodore thomas  blackwood gentleman explorer and  naturalist also known as  scp-1867 his exploits are known far and  wide though some question the validity  of his tales due to the simple fact that  he is a neon sea slug and not a human  man  these are of course fools we have even  covered lord blackwood before in a sea  snails fantasy scp-1867  a gentleman but never before have we  taken a look at such a daring account of  his work today we discuss a most curious  hunting expedition one that brought our  lord blackwood face to face with the  great beast the hard to destroy reptile  scp-682  itself what will become of our hero what  sites will he see on his journey let us  find out tally hall on may 14 1883  months after nearly losing his life  while climbing mount everest lord  blackwood received a letter at his  london home upon opening it he saw that  it was a formal invitation from one  colonel joseph default of the french  army it invited him to participate in a  hunt for a monster known as the terracay  that threatened the lives and security  of the french people anyone who was able  to slay the creature would receive a  handsome award of 5 million pounds for  their trouble unable to resist a  challenge the chance to face off against  a creature he had never heard of before  or the allure of such an impressive  prize lord blackwood sent off an  acceptance so what was the teresque lord  blackwood's research turned up a  fearsome description it was a massive  scaly creature with a high that seemed  impossible to pierce that breathed fire  and killed everything in its path  without batting an eye a worthy foe  indeed by the end of the day lord  blackwood had received an address where  he would attend a briefing before the  hunt would commence the meeting was held  in a private room in the city in an  exclusive club there were three other  would-be hunters there mr roosevelt from  america mr dukoff from russia and mr  harris from england the colonel greeted  the man and told them what they were up  against a beast had laid waste to a  french town ripping men women and  children to shreds and resisting every  blow dealt against it by the army so the  colonel vowed to gather expert  scientists and hunters for if they could  not take down the monster it was likely  that no one could on may the 20th the  party arrived in france to begin the  great adventure each man brought his own  armaments a combination of specialized  weapons and knowledge for the task at  hand the following day the colonel  escorted the man to the quarantine zone  where the beast's attack had led it lord  blackwood was troubled by the sights  there it was a city at war soldiers  patrolled the streets and barricades  were placed at the edge of town citizens  were being evacuated as soldiers aided  them and few had seen the beasts  themselves at least they had not been  unfortunate enough to see it up close  beyond the quarantine barrier it was  hell on earth there were bodies laying  in the streets buildings burnt to the  ground castles and stone walls reduced  to piles of rubble there was not one  living thing in sight not a person a  farm animal or even so much as an insect  the men set up camp near the edge of  town and mr harris set about tracking  the beast before too long he had found  it to the southwest and the next day  they would set off after it the next day  the party made its way southwest to  belleville following a trail of  destruction there they found it having a  nap in the sun it was longer than a  whale taller than a giraffe and bigger  than both lord blackwood thought that if  it had any visible wings he would  consider it a dragon they approached it  slowly careful not to wake the teresque  lord blackwood crouched behind a fence  steadied his gun and fired right at its  head the shot hit and the top of the  teresque's head came off with its impact  it seemed as if the beast was after so  much pomp and circumstance dead right  there but sadly it was not it sprang to  life blood and brains dripping from its  open skull as it turned to the men and  roared then charged the men scattered  firing their guns as they ran the  monster gaining on them faster and  faster until mr ducat fired into its  open wound with an electric rifle it was  stunned long enough for the men to make  it onto their horses as they rode away  the monster continued to chase them new  skin and bone growing over what had once  been a hole in its skull  lord blackwood fired a particle  destabilizer at its leg tearing it off  but as he watched in horror the leg  began to grow back the hunting party  managed to escape with their lives  though their confidence was thoroughly  shaken they rested that night with the  soldiers at the barricade they attempted  to attack the teresque again the  following day but failed once more the  men realized that a simple gunshot  electrocution or fire would not be  enough to kill the monster it simply  healed too fast and its tolerance for  pain was too high in order to kill it  they realized they would have to render  it to mobile and destroy its body so  thoroughly that it would die before it  could rebuild itself and so  they decided to set a trap they dug a  massive trench wide and long enough for  the monster and deep enough that it  would not be able to climb out before  they had killed it in the bottom of the  pit they had placed hundreds of steel  spikes the tips dipped in poison they  placed a bridge across it strong enough  for the men and horses but weak enough  to break under the terrasque's weight  and covered it all with grass and leaves  now they just had to wait mr roosevelt  acted as bait approaching the monster on  horseback and attacking it with a  gunshot then running and leading it back  toward the trap as roosevelt's race  across the bridge the creature pursued  him and fell into the pit where it was  impaled on the spikes then the man  rained down hellfire they shot it with  bullets explosives jellied kerosene mr  duka fired a pitch blend gun that upon  firing released a blur of smoke and fire  once the fire had receded all that  remained was a skeleton the men took the  skull charred from the flames and  planned to take it back as a trophy  all was well or so it seemed the men  returned to the town with the monster  skull in tow and the soldiers cheered at  the site they posed for photographs and  mr dukoff decided to pose with his head  between the jaws of the beast this was a  grave mistake on his part and the jaws  closed tight around his neck his head  falling to the ground the skull acted on  its own rolling and biting all the while  growing fresh skin and scales it opened  its gaping maw and shouted  or for those of you that are not  familiar with the french language you  make me sick screams ran out behind lord  blackwood and he turned to see the rest  of the teresque's body a headless corpse  covered with stringy bits of muscle and  slowly growing brand new flesh it  stomped through the field crushing men  in tents beneath its great feet on its  way to reclaim its head mr harris ran  for the bank vault to grab a weapon he  had only referred to previously as his  secret weapon  lord blackwood chased after him and  found harris pulling a large crate which  he opened with a sense of desperation  there inside was a sarcophagus bound in  chains and covered in ancient ruins  blackwood begged harris to leave the  thing behind and run for his life but he  did not have a chance to finish before  harris opened the lid and an arm  wielding a sword emerged and sliced his  head from his body a man emerged from  the sarcophagus naked wielding a sword  covered in tattoos blackwood had no way  of knowing this but the man was none  other than the deadly warrior  scp-076 or abel the mysterious man  attacked blackwood and roosevelt and  though they tried to defend themselves  no weapon seemed to have an effect on  him he was preparing to deliver a final  blow to blackwood and kill him once and  for all when the terrorscape burst  through the wall of the building with a  mighty bellow at the sight of the  enormous monster abel turned his focus  from the two men to the beast and so the  two seemingly unkillable creatures  driven by bloodlust and inhuman strength  began to fight it took over an hour and  left destruction and death in its wake  abel armed himself with explosives  mounting them to his chest along with  the pitch blend gun and ran towards the  teresque  knowing what would come next roosevelt  and blackwood locked themselves in the  bank vault and prayed that someone would  find them before they starved to death  after two days the men were saved by a  major of the army who was leading a  group of soldiers in search for any  survivors they were taken to a hospital  and nursed back to health by the staff  there as well as a friend of blackwood's  named henry the major who rescued them  told them that the colonel was dead and  so were ten thousand others claimed by  the massive explosion the teresque and  abel had both disappeared and there was  no indication of where either of them  had gone all that was left was  destruction and the memory that a true  monster had made itself known on french  soil now the only thing left to do was  recover as best as anyone could it would  certainly take a very long time the army  was very suspicious of both roosevelt  and blackwood as the only survivors have  an explosion so large it had been seen  throughout france they demanded to know  how the two had survived and what they  had seen throughout this process an  englishman watched and took notes but  did not speak a word roosevelt and  blackwood were eventually released but  they did not receive a penny of their  promised reward and were told they could  not return to france again for the rest  of their lives they were not to speak a  word of what they had seen to anyone or  there would be dire consequences in  calais the two survivors said goodbye  and roosevelt announced he would return  to america to pursue a career in  politics who can say what happened to  him after that upon returning to his  home in london lord blackwood found that  he had received a postcard it read the  royal foundation for the security  containment and protection of anomalous  objects in phantasmagoria requests a  meeting for the purpose of negotiating  an alliance favorable to both our  parties please call anytime except  sundays at number 19 merbonne road  westminster and asked to speak to doctor  thursday your discretion is requested in  this matter he was puzzled by this note  unsure of what to make of it perhaps he  thought he could see what they had to  say after all he was always curious and  ready to explore new territory once he  had recovered sufficiently he would  reach out to this strange group and see  what they might have to offer him and so  began a new chapter of lord blackwood's  story one that included a mysterious  organization called the scp foundation  now go check out a sea snail's fantasy  scp-1867 a gentleman and  scp-682 ways the scp foundation tried to  kill the hard to destroy reptile for  more about the two anomalies featured in  today's thrilling tale
 

